Bugfix: correct lock-free and minimal-lock safety

The Alpha `lock-free` feature no longer turns append operations into dry runs.
`backup`, `copy` destination writes, `merge`, and other append operations now
remain writable and retain their non-exclusive repository lock, so they either
serialize with exclusive `prune`/`forget` work or, with `--retry-lock`, wait and
retry instead of racing pack deletion.

The feature now intentionally applies only to read-only operations (restore,
snapshots, ls, find, dump, repoinfo, ...), which skip lock-file creation.
`--no-lock` remains an explicit operator override for non-exclusive operations.
`check` now uses a read lock because it does not modify repository objects.

The concurrency soak test now requires a durable append snapshot and passes
under `-race`; direct lock-free-read and writable `--no-lock` regressions cover
the corrected behavior. The roadmap accurately marks full rustic-grade
lock-free append / prune-parallel operation as still incomplete.

